extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria printed 41-43 (cache p042-p044, cache page = printed + 1), under the heading Aquatic Races; entry heading Ichthylean R.C.C. The cache text for these pages is out of column order, so every figure was read off 170 dpi renders. The entry ends at Money on printed 43, above the Junk Crab R.C.C. heading. || CATEGORY: a race with its own R.C.C. skills; mdc_base is stated so there is no men_of_arms line. || XP: the entry says Use the Oceanic Guardsman experience table (printed 42); the Experience Tables page (printed 86) heads that column Oceanic Guardsman & Ichthyleans. Stored from a 300 dpi render of printed 86 as the lower bound of each level: 0, 2131, 4261, 8521, 17041, 25041, 35041, 50041, 70041, 95041, 130041, 180041, 230041, 280041, 330041 (level 15 runs to 380,040). No keeps_xp_table: the entry does not say which ladder a mage uses. || ATTRIBUTES as printed: I.Q. 3D6, M.E. 2D6+5, M.A. 1D6+6, P.S. 2D6+18 (Robot), P.P. 2D6+6, P.E. 2D6+6, P.B. 1D6+3, Spd 2D6+10 running. Triple Spd swimming and the 10% fatigue rate are ability text. || POOLS: M.D.C. P.E. x2 to start +1D6 per level as mdc_base; P.P.E. 5D6; Horror Factor 13 (to humans and most D-Bees). The S.D.C.-world figures are ability text. || PSIONICS: all have Empathy (4) and Telepathy (4), granted by name; Telepathy Aquatic Sentient Beings (Special) has no catalog row and is a special ability in prose; considered Major Psychics; I.S.P. M.E. x2 +1D6 per level. The +1D4+1 additional psi-abilities from ONE of Healing, Physical or Sensitive are two pick-one ability groups: one whose three options each carry categories_allowed for a single category, and one whose four options carry powers_starting 2, 3, 4 and 5. The percentile bands on the second group (01-25, 26-50, 51-75, 76-00) are NOT printed; they are the 1D4 spread evenly so the wizard can roll it. || BONUSES are printed per gender and stored on the male and female variants. Males: +1 attack at levels 1, 5 and 10 (in addition to hand to hand), +1 Perception, +1 initiative, +1 disarm and pull punch, +1 save vs Horror Factor at levels 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 and 11. Females: +3 Perception, +1 save vs psionics and magic (stored as spell_magic and ritual_magic), +5% save vs coma/death. Both: -1 save vs poison and drugs, from Vulnerabilities, stored as toxins_poisons and harmful_drugs on the class and restated on each variant because a variant''s bonuses replace the class''s. PROSE ONLY, conditional: automatic dodge underwater only (+2 male, +4 female); the taste/smell-in-water Perception figures (+2 male, +5 female, the female one also for caring for young), read as replacing the general figure rather than adding to it. || SKILLS: Male Ichthylean R.C.C. (97%) and Female Ichthylean R.C.C. (94%) are separate lists, stored as skills_additional on each variant; the two entries both lists share at the same figure (Horsemanship: Aquatic Animals +10%, W.P. Knife) are on the class. base = catalog base + printed bonus, catalog read from production 2026-10-05. Native Language: Ichthylean/Milu is printed at 90% (male) and 92% (female) and keeps the catalog per-level of 2. Language: Lemurian is +10% (male) and +15% (female) but no bonus to speak it; the stored figure is the bonused one over the additional-language base of 50, and its 5 per level is the additional-language rate of the skill description (printed 55), since the page prints a bonus rather than a native-speaker percentage. Track & Hunt Sea Animals is printed with its own figures 35%/25% +5%, which match the catalog row. Underwater Navigation is the catalog Navigation: Underwater; Skin and Prepare Animal Hides is Skin & Prepare Animal Hides; Identify Plants and Fruits is Identify Plants & Fruit. W.P. Ancient (one of choice) and W.P. Modern (two for males, one for females) are choice groups over the catalog rows of each kind; the ancient list leaves out Knife and Trident, which the male list already grants. Swimming 98% is printed under Natural Abilities and is also stored as a skill at 98 with no per-level gain. No related or secondary skills are printed. Hand to Hand: Expert (male) and Basic (female) are printed with no upgrade price, so no hand_to_hand block. || OCCUPATIONS: O.C.C. Note, printed 42: 3% of males and 6% of female Ichthyleans become mages, mostly Ocean Wizards and Sea Druids, but sometimes Biomancer Gene-Mages or other practitioners of magic; and Magic: Rare, by O.C.C. only. Stored as occ_restrictions only group:magic. The book does not say whether a mage keeps the R.C.C. skills (the 97% and 94% in the list headings read as the share who have them), so no pairing_skills; a pairing adds both lists. yields_to_occupation ppe_base to magic is a judgement: the page prints P.P.E. 5D6 beside Magic: Rare, by O.C.C. only, with no wording for a mage''s P.P.E. || MONEY: Salvage and trade goods worth 1D4x1,000 credits (printed 43). The book prints goods, not coin, so no starting_money is stored; the line is kept under restrictions. No equipment is printed. || NOT STORED: size 6 feet + 2D6 inches, weight 200-350 lbs, life span 1D6x10+60 years, gender colouring and 2D4 eggs, disposition, habitat and group sizes, allies and enemies; GM Notes."
