# Ichthylean

## Lore

Ichthyleans are fish-men: scaled from head to foot, with big clawed and webbed hands and feet, a webbed crest of spines down the back and a membrane under each arm. They look like something out of an old monster film, and surface dwellers usually treat them as exactly that. One theory holds that the Lemurians bred them as a trial run for their own aquatic form.

The reputation is undeserved. Among their own and with allies they are gentle, playful and generous, and most want nothing more than a quiet tribal life of hunting, gathering and a little farming under the sea, taking only what they need. They are also strong, fast in the water and psychic to a member, and one that is cornered or defending its young fights without holding back. Centuries of being hunted have made them wary of strangers, and a few tribes have turned to raiding ships and shore villages for supplies, though even raiders avoid killing where they can.

Males and females are raised to different work. Males are the hunters, trackers and fighters; females tend the farms, the animals, the sick and the food stores, and are the sharper-eyed of the two. A small number of either sex leave that path to study magic.

## GM Notes

Also called Ichthys, Lee-anns and Water Lions. Size 6 feet plus 2D6 inches (1.8 to 2.1 m); weight 200 to 350 lbs (90 to 157 kg), all muscle and blubber. Life span 1D6x10+60 years, physically mature at 10. Males are a rich green with blue accents and coloured fins; females are a lighter green with yellow webbing and fins and a head-to-spine crest twice the male''s size in orange or red. Females lay 2D4 eggs, which are watched in a nest for four months.

Habitat: waters worldwide, preferring the Pacific and other warm seas, with some in the waterways of the Americas, Africa, India and Southeast Asia and a few in deep lakes, swamps and jungle rivers. They avoid the mid-Atlantic, where Splugorth Slavers and Metztla hunt them. Met as a lone hunter, a pair, a small family or a hunting party of up to 1D6+2; a typical village holds 2D6x10, a large one 5D6x10.

Allies: Lemurians, whom they regard as brothers and often live beside, and cetaceans. Several other groups are judged one by one and mostly met with uneasy indifference: Sea Druids and Ocean Wizards, Amphibs, Junk Crabs, the Milu, Merans, and the New Navy as well. The humans of Tritonia are distrusted. Enemies: demons and the undead, the Naut''Yll, Horune Pirates, the Lord of the Deep, and the Splugorth together with their minions. About 75% believe all surface dwellers are cruel, whatever the Lemurians say.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ichthylean');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ichthylean';

